# Elderly Pursuits (otherAreas 75): Para popped twice in one flow, the corpse's despawn run while the char is in another
# zone. Accepted at Prog 1 with the amulet: the ??? pops Para; the kill: Prog 2. A warp to Southern San d'Oria
# (onZoneOut at Prog 2: Prog 1). Carpenters' Landing keeps ticking with nobody in it. The ticks are cut to the ms: the
# kill's second 1 s tick and the warp's 400 ms come after the death, so 13601 ms more puts the clock 15001 ms after it,
# past the 15 s death state (the test is strict: a tick at exactly 15000 ms would not end it), and the 3 s fade-out
# begins (CDespawnState). After the 2600 ms tick Para is still fading; the warp back's own 400 ms tick reaches the 3 s
# and it fades out. A tick runs the zones once, as the C++ test simulation's skipTime does, so a corpse's despawn takes
# two ticks (one long tick leaves it fading). Back at Prog 1: the ??? pops Para again, and the second kill: Prog 2.
lists CarpentersLanding/onZoneOut/1 CarpentersLanding/qm_para/onTrigger CarpentersLanding/Para/onMobDeath
char zone=CarpentersLanding pos=-414.6,0,-363.5 job=WAR lvl=75
quest OtherAreas.SecretsOfOvensLost completed
quest OtherAreas.ElderlyPursuits accepted
charvar Quest[4][75]Prog 1
keyitem AntiqueAmulet
login
trigger qm_para                         # Prog 1: Para popped
kill PARA                               # Prog 2
warp -14.7,2.1,11.8 SouthernSanDoria    # onZoneOut at Prog 2: Prog 1
tick 13601                              # 15001 ms after the death (strict): the fade-out begins
tick 2600                               # 2600 ms into the fade: still fading
warp -414.6,0,-363.5 CarpentersLanding  # its 400 ms tick: 3 s into the fade, Para fades out
trigger qm_para                         # Prog 1: Para popped again
kill PARA                               # Prog 2
